<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Perry Point</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:217-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.373973" lon="-121.566853"><ele>1008.3</ele><name>Highway 35 at Road 44</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hwy35-road-44 (OSM node 33436785); confidence: high; pdf_page: 214; book_elev_ft: 3280; quote: All tours in this area are reached by skiing (or driving) uphill on Road 44 from Highway 35 ... (3,280 feet)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.408084" lon="-121.546922"><ele>1306.3</ele><name>Road 44 / Road 4410 junction, 200 yd past Clinger Spring</name><desc>source: OSM node 33426868, as in or-vielbig-2e_218-1; OSM Clinger Spring node 45.408783,-121.550818 is 300 m west; confidence: high; pdf_page: 214; book_elev_ft: 4200; quote: Clinger Spring itself is 1,000 feet above and 3.6 miles from Highway 35.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.416224" lon="-121.525894"><ele>1302.4</ele><name>Road 44 / Road 17 junction (the book's 44/1720 junction), south end of Brooks Meadow</name><desc>source: OSM node 33437099, where NF 44 turns east (Dufur Valley Road) and NF 17 ('Brooks Meadow Road') goes north along the meadow's west side; 1.47 mi by Road 44 from the 4410 junction. Today's 17/1720 junction (node 33428671) is 0.45 mi further north at the meadow's north end: the book's text puts its junction at the south end, with Road 17 along the meadow's west side reaching it; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 217; book_elev_ft: 4280; quote: From Clinger Spring continue on Road 44 1.5 miles, or better yet ski the more interesting Surveyor Trail to the Road 44/1720 junction. Enter the trees straight ahead to locate nearby Brooks Meadow. ... go to the junction of Roads 44 and 1720 at the south end of Brooks Meadow.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.394772" lon="-121.507325"><ele>1418.7</ele><name>Knebal Pass (Road 44 high point)</name><desc>source: OSM node 33416308 on NF 44 (Dufur Valley Road), 1.87 mi by road from node 33437099; DEM high point of the road, 4,655 ft; the road falls east of it; confidence: high; pdf_page: 218; book_elev_ft: 4680; quote: This 4,680-foot pass lies 1.9 miles southeast of Brooks Meadow (and 7 miles from Highway 35) on Road 44, a gentle climb of 440 feet.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.394730" lon="-121.499222"><ele>1388.5</ele><name>Road 44 / side road NF 1720-120 (to Fivemile Butte)</name><desc>source: OSM node 4274764377, 0.40 mi east of Knebal Pass by Road 44 (downhill), where NF 1720-120 leaves north for Fivemile Butte; Bottle Prairie Trail #455 starts 40 m away (node 14150181032); confidence: high; pdf_page: 219; quote: ski east 0.4 mile downhill from Knebal Pass to an obvious side road on the left (north) side of Road 44.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.402668" lon="-121.492944"><ele>1486.0</ele><name>Bottle Prairie Trail #455 below Perry Point</name><desc>source: OSM node 471273852 on Bottle Prairie Trail #455, 0.72 mi up the trail; the trail climbs the ridge from Road 44 and passes 40 m from the GNIS Perry Point (node 357313402, 45.403172,-121.492851). Read as the book's primitive road; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 219; quote: leave it quickly and climb into a nearby opening. Turn right (east) and climb through a meadow into forest following a primitive road. Continue through clearings and forest to sidehill meadows with great views south and east.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.403200" lon="-121.491700"><ele>1500.8</ele><name>Perry Point, far east end of the ridge</name><desc>source: placed from the DEM: the ridge runs west to east past GNIS Perry Point and ends at about 4,920 ft where it falls steeply east; sketch 4920'; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 219; book_elev_ft: 4920; quote: Go to the far end of the ridge (1.2 miles from Knebal Pass), where you will enjoy the beauty of the craggy, snow-drifted narrow point with weathered, twisted pines.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Perry Point</name><desc>1. Highway 35 at Road 44 -&gt; Road 44 / Road 4410 junction, 200 yd past Clinger Spring: osm (high), 3.78 mi | 2. Road 44 / Road 4410 junction, 200 yd past Clinger Spring -&gt; Road 44 / Road 17 junction (the book's 44/1720 junction), south end of Brooks Meadow: osm (high), 1.45 mi | 3. Road 44 / Road 17 junction (the book's 44/1720 junction), south end of Brooks Meadow -&gt; Knebal Pass (Road 44 high point): osm (high), 1.87 mi | 4. Knebal Pass (Road 44 high point) -&gt; Road 44 / side road NF 1720-120 (to Fivemile Butte): osm (high), 0.40 mi | 5. Road 44 / side road NF 1720-120 (to Fivemile Butte) -&gt; Bottle Prairie Trail #455 below Perry Point: osm (medium), 0.76 mi | 6. Bottle Prairie Trail #455 below Perry Point -&gt; Perry Point, far east end of the ridge: straight (medium), 0.07 mi</desc>
